  "narrative": "The first discovery screen produced four claims with large signed effects far from zero: H8, H9, and H12 supported their registered directions, while H7 supported the opposite direction. Using the claim-card signed estimates, positive values indicate evidence toward the registered direction; negative values indicate evidence away from it. H8 (MSI-high versus MSS for WRN dependency) had a positive signed mean_difference of 0.790 (95% CI 0.760 to 0.819), H9 (SMARCA4 loss for SMARCA2 dependency) had 0.784 (0.765 to 0.803), and H12 (TP53 intact versus TP53 loss for USP7 dependency) had 0.396 (0.325 to 0.467). These intervals exclude zero and are large relative to the outcome scales and the 10% clinical-significance benchmark, so I accept them as dataset-supported associations, while retaining that this is not proof of causal essentiality or external generalizability. H7 is striking in the opposite direction: the signed estimate is -0.796 (-0.816 to -0.776), meaning KEAP1-loss is not associated with stronger negative dependency_NFE2L2 but instead with the opposite direction in this dataset. I reject the original H7 claim and request validation of H7 to test whether this surprising opposite direction is stable before accepting a reversed claim. The driver-mutation/amplification hypotheses were mostly weak. H1 was positive but small and statistically non-significant, so I leave it unresolved rather than accept; H5 is borderline positive near a 10% relative-scale effect but its 95% interval still crosses zero, so it remains unresolved and gets a KRAS-wild-type follow-up because EGFR and KRAS alterations can define related but overlapping subpopulations. H4 supports less KRAS dependency in BRAF-mutant cells but is small and non-significant, so unresolved. H2, H6, H10, and H11 are either very small or cross zero, and do not support their claims. Multiplicity is manageable given the pre-specified 12-test panel, but I still avoid accepting borderline effects such as H5. I register follow-up interaction tests for accepted effects and negative-control marker tests using constructed research markers with no assigned biological role.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-supported associations so far: H8 MSI-high increases WRN dependency; H9 SMARCA4 loss increases SMARCA2 dependency; H12 TP53-intact status increases USP7 dependency. H7 is rejected in original direction but shows a large opposite effect; validating H7 before accepting reversal. Next priorities: (1) independent validation of H7 to test stability of the opposite NFE2L2 direction; (2) EGFR amplification effect restricted to KRAS-wild-type cells; (3) effect-modification tests for SMARCA4-SMARCA2 and TP53-USP7 associations; (4) negative-control comparisons with research markers D/E to check false-positive inflation. Keep causal and generalizability claims narrow; treat results as associations within the supplied screen dataset unless independent validation and broader evidence support stronger conclusions.",
