istic guess and should be described as a measured association rather than causal confirmation. These main effects are supported by independent validation and are stable across major tested strata, including adenocarcinoma, batch_a, Avana for WRN, KY for SMARCA2 and NFE2L2, and KY for USP7. Formal interactions for lineage subtype and TP53 status were small and null. Negative controls and TMED10 specificity probes are null, arguing against a simple assay artifact or broad MSI confound. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in smaller or imprecise comparisons: KRAS-mutation effects on KRAS, BRAF, STAT3, and USP7; EGFR-amplification effects on EGFR dependency; ARID1A-context modifiers of SMARCA2; MYC amplification effects on POLR2A/KIF18A; and BRCA2-loss effects on DHX9. No further validation is needed for the four main effects or for H64; validation should be reserved if a new large, unvalidated robust association emerges. The next analyses should run the active registered KRAS/BRAF/STK11, ARID1A/SMARCA2, USP7/KRAS modifier, MYC/transcription-replication, BRCA2/DHX9, and EGFR-dependency comparisons to map the boundary of the robust findings rather than retesting the main effects.",
