s +0.013 (independent adjusted CI -0.031 to +0.058, R80). Both intervals cross zero and the point estimates are small relative to the TMED10 score distribution. I keep H67 rejected and closed.\n\nWith these results, the dataset-supported robust associations are now: MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; TP53-intact status is associated with stronger USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency relative to KEAP1-intact cells; and PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency. Prior accepted context results for lineage subtype, screen batch, library, and ARID1A-stratified SMARCA4/SMARCA2 remain concordant with their main effects. I close the main investigations and accepted context investigations for H9, H13, H39, H45-H51 because the main effects are validated and these direct strata were precise and concordant, while keeping unresolved context checks such as H87-H89 and the newly registered TP53-stratum PTEN checks active for further characterization. The next analyses should prioritize PTEN/STAT3 stability by TP53 and PIK3CA status, the still-untested ARID1A-loss main contrast H61, and remaining active unresolved predictors, while preserving validation capacity for any new large robust discovery rather than spending it on imprecise small-effect modifiers.",
