  "narrative": "All newly returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so a positive signed estimate supports the registered claim and a negative signed estimate opposes it. The PTEN-loss/dependency_STAT3 association is again strongly supported: in SMAD4-intact cells, H117 gives +0.259 (95% CI +0.205 to +0.313; R121), and in adherent growth-pattern cells, H123 gives +0.262 (95% CI +0.203 to +0.321; R127). These are meaningful on the dependency-score scale, interval-excluding-zero, and consistent with the already validated overall PTEN/STAT3 result and several context-specific accepted subgroup results. I accept both as dataset-supported context robustness checks and close them. The MSI-high/WRN association persists in TP53-intact cells: H122 gives +0.780 (95% CI +0.747 to +0.813; R126), an enormous effect relative to the dependency scale, so I accept and close H122. KEAP1-loss/dependency_NFE2L2 is similarly robust: H42 in TP53-intact cells gives +0.792 (95% CI +0.770 to +0.815; R128), and H43 in TP53-loss cells gives +0.810 (95% CI +0.763 to +0.857; R129). Both are far larger than practical relevance thresholds and interval-excluding-zero; I accept them. TP53-intact/dependency_USP7 is also supported separately in KRAS-mutant and KRAS-wild-type cells: H40 gives +0.410 (95% CI +0.260 to +0.561; R131), and H41 gives +0.392 (95% CI +0.311 to +0.473; R132). These are substantial effects and close out the KRAS context checks. The new formal interaction H118, testing whether the PTEN-loss/STAT3 effect is attenuated in TP53-loss cells, has a positive point estimate +0.097 but a 95% interval that crosses zero (-0.024 to +0.217; R122). This is not sufficient to accept modification, but because the point estimate is near the lower boundary of practical relevance and the interval includes moderate positive values, I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than rejecting it as exactly null. The two new p53-pathway probes for MDM2 and RPL11 do not support the registered hypotheses. H34, overall CDKN2A loss with dependency_MDM2 direction +1, gives a negative signed effect -0.117 (95% CI -0.152 to -0.082; R130), meaning the raw association is opposite the registered positive hypothesis and interval-excluding-zero. H119, the same predictor restricted to TP53-intact cells, also gives a negative signed effect -0.119 (95% CI -0.158 to -0.079; R123). Thus the registered CDKN2A-loss/MDM2-positive hypotheses are rejected. The data do point consistently toward the opposite sign, but because that reversal was not the registered claim, I treat it as post hoc hypothesis generation rather than an accepted claim. The MYC/RPL11 probes are null: H120 gives -0.009 (95% CI -0.034 to +0.015; R124), and the TP53-loss interaction H121 gives +0.016 (95% CI -0.038 to +0.069; R125); both interval-crossing and negligible in size. I do not request independent validation this iteration because the newly accepted findings corroborate already accepted and mostly already validated main associations, while the CDKN2A/MDM2 reversal is a post-hoc sign change that should be registered explicitly before being accepted or validated. These remain associations in this supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence after current discovery batch. The five strongest dataset-supported associations remain: (1) MSI-high -> much stronger dependency_WRN: main R8/R39; now also robust in TP53-intact cells R126; previously robust in adenocarcinoma R27, batch_a R28, Avana R41, KY R105; lineage/batch interactions null R49/R19. (2) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency_SMARCA2: main R9/R26; ARID1A-intact R75, ARID1A-loss validated R65/R66, adenocarcinoma R32, batch_a R29, KY R42, TP53-loss R114; many interactions null/rejected. (3) TP53-intact -> stronger dependency_USP7: main R12/R40; adenocarcinoma R34, batch_a R30, KY validated R43/R53, STK11-loss R113; now separately supported in KRAS-mutant cells R131 and KRAS-wild-type cells R132; KRAS/lineage/batch/KEAP1/PIK3CA interactions mostly null/rejected. (4) KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative dependency_NFE2L2: main R7/R13; adenocarcinoma R33, batch_a R31, KY R44, STK11-loss R112; now robust in TP53-intact cells R128 and TP53-loss cells R129; lineage/TP53-intact interactions null R51/R52; KEAP1 overall STAT3 null R108. (5) PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3: main R73/R79; adenocarcinoma R81, TP53-intact R84, TP53-loss validated R85/R93, KEAP1-loss R102, KY validated R101/R106, batch_a R109, Avana R110, STK11-loss validated R111/R120; now robust in SMAD4-intact cells R121 and adherent growth-pattern cells R127; lineage/KRAS/PIK3CA interactions and alternative outcomes mostly null. New negative/null results: H120 MYC amplification in TP53-intact cells for dependency_RPL11 is interval-crossing and negligible R124; H121 MYC/RPL11 interaction by TP53 loss is interval-crossing and negligible R125. H118 PTEN/STAT3 interaction by TP53 loss is positive but interval-crossing (+0.097, CI -0.024 to +0.217; R122), so left unresolved/deferred. The CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2 probes reject the registered positive hypothesis: overall R130 and TP53-intact R123 both show negative signed effects around -0.118 with intervals excluding zero. This suggests an opposite association (CDKN2A loss associated with stronger/more-negative MDM2 dependency) in this dataset, but it was not the registered direction and should be registered as a new claim if pursued. H98 remains deferred due insufficient PTEN-loss by SMAD4-loss interaction cell count; H117 instead provides a feasible SMAD4-intact context check. No validation requested this iteration; one voluntary validation request remains. Reserve validation for a future formally registered high-value reversal or unresolved robustness check, not for context confirmations of already accepted main associations."
