  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support a stronger dependency direction when the registered direction is -1 and support the registered interaction contrast when the registered contrast is interaction. The two due validations are decisive. H113 tests PTEN loss versus no PTEN loss within STK11-loss cells for dependency_STAT3. Discovery gave signed +0.258, 95% CI +0.134 to +0.382, and independent validation gave +0.339, adjusted CI +0.122 to +0.557. The validated lower bound exceeds the practical 0.1-dependency-score-unit benchmark used here, and the interval excludes zero with a large point estimate. I therefore accept H113 and close it. This strengthens the PTEN-loss dependency_STAT3 association beyond the main population, TP53-loss cells, and the smaller KY library, showing that it remains strong in Avana-library STK11-loss cells. H124 tests the newly reversed CDKN2A-loss association with dependency_MDM2 in the overall eligible population. Discovery gave signed +0.117, 95% CI +0.082 to +0.152, meaning CDKN2A-loss cells have more-negative dependency_MDM2 scores, i.e. stronger MDM2 dependency. Independent validation gave +0.132, adjusted CI +0.080 to +0.184. The lower bound is slightly below the practical 0.1 threshold, but the replicated point estimate exceeds it, the adjusted interval excludes zero, and the effect is consistent with TP53-intact, TP53-loss, and batch_a strata. I therefore accept H124 and close it as a moderate but replicated dataset association. With these validations, the dataset-supported main associations are now: MSI-high is associated with much stronger dependency_WRN; SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency_SMARCA2; TP53-intact status is associated with stronger dependency_USP7; KEAP1 loss is associated with less-negative and therefore weaker dependency_NFE2L2; PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency_STAT3; and CDKN2A loss is associated 