  "narrative": "No new validation can be requested because the independent-validation budget is exhausted, so I did not set validate. All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the direction -1 contrasts (MSI-high/dependency_WRN, SMARCA4-loss/dependency_SMARCA2, TP53-intact/dependency_USP7, PTEN-loss/dependency_STAT3, CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2), a positive signed estimate means the exposed category has a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. For H199, direction +1 was registered for KEAP1-loss versus KEAP1-intact dependency_NFE2L2; a positive signed estimate therefore means less negative NFE2L2 scores in KEAP1-loss cells, i.e. weaker apparent dependency, consistent with the previously accepted reversal.\n\nH196 through H199 are low-Cas9-activity complements of four accepted core associations. H196 MSI-high/dependency_WRN gives +0.811 (95% CI +0.767 to +0.854, n 59 and 794). H197 SMARCA4-loss/dependency_SMARCA2 gives +0.771 (CI +0.742 to +0.801, n 174 and 679). H198 TP53-intact/dependency_USP7 gives +0.408 (CI +0.301 to +0.515, n 676 and 177). H199 KEAP1-loss/weaker dependency_NFE2L2 gives +0.797 (CI +0.766 to +0.828, n 168 and 685). All four have enormous point estimates, lower bounds far above the practical 0.1 dependency-score benchmark, and adequate cells. These results support the conclusion that the associations are not artifacts confined to the best Cas9-activity screens in this dataset. Because these are same-data technical robustness checks and validation capacity is exhausted, I accept and close them as robustness evidence, not as independent external replication.\n\nThe PTEN-loss/dependency_STAT3 context checks are uniformly supportive. H201 low Cas9 gives +0.271 (CI +0.194 to +0.349, n 130 and 723). H202 high screen ROC gives +0.253 (CI +0.181 to +0.325, n 123 and 881). H203 low screen ROC gives +0.280 (CI +0.205 to +0.355, n 143 and 853). H205 media serum at least 10 gives +0.286 (CI +0.216 to +0.357, n 158 and 1022). H206 media serum at most 5 gives +0.239 (CI +0.163 to +0.316, n 108 and 712). All five lower bounds exceed the practical benchmark, cell sizes are adequate, and the directions are consistent with the accepted main PTEN-loss/STAT3 effect. Thus the association appears broad across Cas9 activity, screen ROC AUC, and serum-serum level in this dataset. I accept and close these as context robustness checks.\n\nThe CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2 checks are the important caution. H200 low Cas9 gives +0.092 (CI +0.042 to +0.142). H204 RNA+WGS gives +0.096 (CI +0.054 to +0.138). H207 low screen ROC gives +0.103 (CI +0.056 to +0.150). These are directionally consistent with the accepted main and independently validated CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2 association, and none is near the null. However, the point estimates hover around the practical 0.1 benchmark and the lower bounds are clearly below it. This means the data are consistent with a positive association in these technical subsets, but they do not robustly establish a scientifically meaningful subset-specific effect above the benchmark. I therefore leave H200, H204, and H207 unresolved and deferred rather than accept them as confirmed subset effects. This does not reject the main CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2 association, which was already accepted on discovery plus independent validation; it only prevents overclaiming about low-Cas9, RNA+WGS, or low-screen-quality subsets. To clarify whether the main effect is attenuated in weaker screens or broad across screen quality, I registered high-Cas9 and high-screen-ROC direct complement tests for CDKN2A-loss/dependency_MDM2.\n\nMultiplicity and overlapping strata were considered. Many accepted context tests are highly correlated or partition the same population. The accepted results are large and interval-supported, so multiplicity is not a major concern there. The borderline CDKN2A/MDM2 context results are treated conservatively because their uncertainty intervals do not robustly exceed the practical threshold. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations within this supplied lung CRISPR screen dataset; none establishes causality, therapeutic vulnerability, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "ITERATION 17 APPRAISE. No validation remains. New discovery results complete low-Cas9 complements for five core associations plus screen ROC/serum context for PTEN-loss/STAT3 and technical context for CDKN2A-loss/MDM2. Interpret signed estimates: for direction -1, positive means stronger dependency in exposed; for H199 direction +1, positive means weaker apparent NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss.\n\nAccepted/closed now: H196 MSI-high/WRN low Cas9 +0.811; H197 SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 low Cas9 +0.771; H198 TP53-intact/USP7 low Cas9 +0.408; H199 KEAP1-loss/weaker NFE2L2 low Cas9 +0.797; H201 PTEN-loss/STAT3 low Cas9 +0.271; H202 PTEN-loss/STAT3 high ROC +0.253; H203 PTEN-loss/STAT3 low ROC +0.280; H205 PTEN-loss/STAT3 serum>=10 +0.286; H206 PTEN-loss/STAT3 serum<=5 +0.239. These further support broad, technically robust dataset associations.\n\nBorderline CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 context tests left unresolved/deferred: H200 low Cas9 +0.092 CI 0.042-0.142; H204 RNA+WGS +0.096 CI 0.054-0.138; H207 low ROC +0.103 CI 0.056-0.150. Main CDKN2A/MDM2 remains accepted from H124/main validation; subset-specific >0.1 not robustly demonstrated. Proposed high Cas9 MDM2 and high ROC MDM2 direct complements to clarify screen-quality dependence. H194 low IFN + TP53-intact PTEN/STAT3 and H195 media>=9 PTEN/STAT3 remain active untested but lower priority than high-Cas9/high-ROC MDM2 complements. Final accepted primary associations remain MSI-high/WRN, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, TP53-intact/USP7, KEAP1-loss/weaker NFE2L2, PTEN-loss/STAT3, and CDKN2A-loss/MDM2; all are dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
