ncy_STAT3 in low screen-quality and low-Cas9 cells, strengthening the technical robustness of the main PTEN/STAT3 association. H258 rejects a practical CDKN2A-loss association with dependency_MDM2 in high screen-quality, low-Cas9, MTAP-intact cells: signed estimate is 0.037 and the interval includes zero. This does not overturn the validated main CDKN2A/MDM2 effect, but it does not certify this QC/MTAP context. H259 through H262 accept the four core accepted associations in low screen-quality and low-Cas9 cells: MSI-high stronger dependency_WRN, SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency_SMARCA2, TP53 intact stronger dependency_USP7, and KEAP1 loss weaker apparent dependency_NFE2L2. Their lower confidence limits are very far above the practical benchmark. Overall, these results reinforce technical robustness of core effects and PTEN/STAT3 context, reject independent MTAP effects, and keep CDKN2A/MDM2 subgroup-specific QC contexts unresolved or rejected when lower bounds do not clear the practical rule. No conclusions here are causal or generalizable; they are descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, subject to multiplicity, missing Cas9-activity observations, and possible confounding by co-occurring genomic alterations or selection induced by QC eligibility. I registered one additional proposal to complete the CDKN2A/MDM2 technical-quality matrix in low-screen, high-Cas9, MTAP-intact cells; this remains only a dataset-specific follow-up.",
