parent NFE2L2 dependency, interpreted as less negative dependency scores, H13/R7 estimate 0.796, 0.776 to 0.816, validated by R13 estimate 0.781, 0.752 to 0.809; it remains large across screen_nnmd strata, R276 estimate 0.793 lower bound 0.764 and R277 estimate 0.799 lower bound 0.771. PTEN-loss cells have stronger STAT3 dependency, H85/R73 estimate 0.267, 0.215 to 0.319, validated by R79 estimate 0.274, 0.200 to 0.348; this is the broadest accepted context association, with many accepted direct strata across TP53, KRAS, lineage, growth pattern, mutation burden, aneuploidy, IFN-gamma, hypoxia, EMT, screen quality, Cas9 activity, and screen_nnmd, for example R138, R169, R262, R263, R252, R264, R278 lower bound 0.247 and R279 lower bound 0.139. CDKN2A-loss cells have stronger MDM2 dependency, accepted as H124/R130 estimate 0.117, 0.082 to 0.152 and validated by R143 estimate 0.132, 0.080 to 0.184, though this is the smallest accepted effect and the earlier opposite-direction H34 remains rejected. Context stability: the four largest core effects are robust to technical screen-quality and Cas9-activity splits, and the new screen_nnmd direct strata support stability for WRN, SMARCA2, USP7, NFE2L2, and STAT3. However, stability of direct strata does not certify a general interaction model. Many interaction tests were imprecise or null, including H226 screen-quality interaction for STAT3/PTEN rejected by R241, H224 high-screen IFN interaction unresolved with R239 crossing zero, and most WRN, SMARCA2, USP7, and NFE2L2 interactions rejected. CDKN2A/MDM2 screen_nnmd strata remain unresolved because R280 lower bound 0.060 and R281 lower bound 0.075 fall below the practical benchmark. Negative findings: canonical driver concordance is absent or negligible in this dataset, KRAS mutation does not predict dependency_KRAS, R1 estimate 0.014, BRAF V600E does not predict dependency_BRAF, R3 estimate -0.017, EGFR amplification does not predict dependency_EGFR, R5 estimate 0.025, and E