  "narrative": "Independent validation is exhausted and no claim assessments are due, so the remaining exploration should focus on resolving the most important unresolved interaction and attribution questions rather than accumulating more one-way accepted strata. First, for PTEN-loss and dependency_STAT3, the main effect and many direct strata are accepted, but the IFN-gamma interaction structure remains incomplete: full-population IFN>=0.5 and low-screen IFN>=0.5 interaction evidence are supportive, high-screen IFN>=0.5 is unresolved, and IFN>=0 interactions are weaker. I therefore propose a high-screen IFN>=0 interaction. Under direction -1, a positive signed estimate means the PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency effect is more negative, i.e. stronger, in IFN-positive high-screen cells than in IFN-negative high-screen cells. If this clears about 0.1 absolute dependency-score units, it would suggest a broader IFN-related effect modification in high-quality screens; if not, the IFN interaction may remain restricted to lower screen-quality or higher IFN-threshold contexts. Second, the validated MDM2 effect associated with CDKN2A loss is the smallest accepted core effect and its attribution to CDKN2A versus co-occurring MTAP loss remains uncertain. I propose direct CDKN2A effects in TP53-intact MTAP-intact and TP53-intact MTAP-loss cells, a direct MTAP effect within CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact cells, and an interaction between CDKN2A and MTAP within TP53-intact cells. For the direct CDKN2A claims, direction -1 means a positive signed estimate supports stronger MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells. For the MTAP direct claim, direction -1 means positive supports stronger MDM2 dependency with MTAP loss, but the expected direction is uncertain. For the CDKN2A-by-MTAP interaction, direction +1 means positive signed evidence corresponds to a raw interaction in which the CDKN2A effect is less negative, or more attenuated, among MTAP-loss cells relative to MTAP-intact cells. This pattern would support MTAP co-loss or pathway interaction as an important confounder or modifier; an interaction near zero would support CDKN2A as the primary measured predictor in TP53-intact cells. Third, although accepted core effects are generally robust in direct screen-quality strata, effect modification by high Cas9 activity remains less fully characterized. I add interactions at cas9_activity_pct>=85 for STAT3/PTEN, MDM2/CDKN2A, and USP7/TP53-intact. For these direction -1 claims, positive signed estimates mean stronger dependency-score contrasts in high-Cas9 cells than in lower-Cas9 cells. Large positive interactions would indicate technical Cas9 dependence; null or small interactions would support context stability, while strong negative interactions would suggest stronger effects in lower-Cas9 cells. These are all dataset-specific association hypotheses, not causal or generalizability claims. Because many overlapping subgroup tests have been performed, I will continue to use about 0.1 absolute dependency-score units as a conservative practical benchmark, accepting only estimates whose signed lower confidence bound clearly exceeds that threshold for the relevant direction, rejecting small or null-crossing effects, and leaving compatible but sub-threshold estimates unresolved.",
