{
  "narrative": "Final synthesis: No new validation results arrived at this stage, assessments_due is empty, and the independent validation budget is exhausted. All cited estimates are already signed to the registered claim direction and are interpreted without further re-signing. Given continuous dependency scores that can be negative, the stated 10 percent relative threshold was operationalized conservatively as an approximate 0.1 absolute dependency-unit lower-bound practical benchmark, with validated main effects accepted when supported by independent replication even when smaller direct-stratum estimates remained below that threshold. The conclusions below are descriptive associations in the supplied 2000-cell lung, adenocarcinoma-heavy dataset, not causal statements and not generalization guarantees.\\n\\nSupported core findings. First, MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency: H8/R8 estimate 0.790, 95 percent interval 0.760 to 0.819, independently validated by R39 estimate 0.771, interval 0.720 to 0.822. It persists across technical strata, including screen_nnmd splits R270 and R271 and strict screen-quality or Cas9 strata R254 and R266, and across many genomic subgroups. Second, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H9/R9 estimate 0.784, interval 0.765 to 0.803, validated by R26 estimate 0.807, interval 0.777 to 0.838. This holds in ARID1A-intact cells R75 and ARID1A co-loss cells R65, with the ARID1A co-loss subset validated by R66, and is descriptively stable across screen_nnmd strata R272 and R273 and strict QC strata R255 and R267. Third, TP53-intact status is associated with stronger USP7 dependency than TP53 loss: H12/R12 estimate 0.396, interval 0.325 to 0.467, validated by R40 estimate 0.435, interval 0.334 to 0.536. It persists in KRAS-mutant R131 and KRAS wild-type R132 cells and across screen_nnmd strata R274 and R275 and strict QC strata R256 and R268; the smaller Ky-library stratum remains accepted and validated by R53. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with higher, less negative, apparent NFE2L2 dependency scores, meaning weaker apparent dependency: H13/R7 estimate 0.796, interval 0.776 to 0.816, validated by R13 estimate 0.781, interval 0.752 to 0.809; this also remains large across screen_nnmd strata R276 and R277 and strict QC strata R257 and R269. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H85/R73 estimate 0.267, interval 0.215 to 0.319, validated by R79 estimate 0.274, interval 0.200 to 0.348. This is the broadest accepted context association, with many accepted direct strata across TP53, KRAS, lineage, growth pattern, mutation burden, aneuploidy, IFN-gamma, hypoxia, EMT, screen quality, Cas9 activity, and screen_nnmd, for example R138, R169, R220, R262, R263, R252, R264, R278, and R279. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H124/R130 estimate 0.117, interval 0.082 to 0.152, validated by R143 estimate 0.132, interval 0.080 to 0.184. This is the smallest accepted core effect and is not fully attributed to co-occurring MTAP status.\\n\\nContext and specificity. Several negative findings clarify specificity. Canonical driver concordance is absent: KRAS mutation does not predict dependency_KRAS in a practical direction, R1 estimate 0.014 with interval -0.004 to 0.031; BRAF V600E does not predict dependency_BRAF, R3 estimate -0.017, interval -0.045 to 0.012; EGFR amplification does not predict dependency_EGFR, R5 estimate 0.025, interval -0.000 to 0.051; ERBB2 amplification does not predict dependency_ERBB2, R6 estimate 0.001, interval -0.027 to 0.030. TP53 loss alone is not a practical predictor of MDM2 R11, STAT3 R100, WRN R165, or RPL11 R90. MYC amplification is null or below practical thresholds across RPL11 R21, POLR2A R116, KIF18A R78, TMED10 R45, DHX9 R64, MDM2 R136, SMARCA2 R147, and WRN R235, where R235 is a small opposite-direction estimate. ARID1A loss is not a practical independent SMARCA2 marker, R86, and is not practical within SMARCA4-loss cells, R164. PTEN specificity is supported because PTEN loss is not practical for USP7 R103, MDM2 R104, or WRN R173. MTAP loss is not a robust independent predictor: MTAP main effects are small or null for MDM2 R176, STAT3 R260, and USP7 R261; MTAP within CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact cells is not practical R285; and the MTAP attenuation interaction for CDKN2A is not supported R286. Research markers D, E, and F behaved as null or practically insignificant assay controls, for example R15, R17, R142, R24, R25, R35, R118, and R141.\\n\\nUnresolved uncertainty. The strongest residual uncertainty is attribution of the validated CDKN2A-MDM2 association. Direct subset estimates are directionally compatible but do not clear the conservative lower-bound benchmark: TP53-intact CDKN2A estimates include R123 lower 0.079, R283 lower 0.063, and R284 lower 0.070; MTAP stratified estimates include R248 lower 0.081 and R249 lower 0.067; strict technical subsets can be subthreshold or null, for example R259 lower 0.060 and R265 crossing zero. These do not overturn the validated main effect but prevent acceptance of MTAP co-loss as a practical independent driver or modifier, while small modification cannot be fully excluded. IFN-gamma interaction structure for PTEN loss and STAT3 dependency remains incomplete: accepted IFN-gamma interactions include R144 for IFN-gamma at least 0.5, R157 for IFN-gamma at least 0.66, and the lower-screen interaction R225, but high-screen interactions R239 and R282 remain zero-crossing and unresolved. Other unresolved issues include some lower-bound direct strata such as R179 and some CDKN2A screen_nnmd strata R280 and R281. Interaction tests for WRN, SMARCA2, USP7, and NFE2L2 mostly failed to show practical modification, and screen_nnmd interactions R290 through R293 were rejected as practical effects. Some claims lacked valid cells, such as R119 and R148, and were not used as evidence.\\n\\nOverall conclusion and next analysis. The evidence supports six dataset-specific associations: MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53-intact status with stronger USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker apparent NFE2L2 dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency. The first four are very large and robust across many splits within this dataset; STAT3/PTEN is moderately large and broad; MDM2/CDKN2A is validated but smaller and attributionally uncertain. The most informative next analysis is external held-out replication of these six core associations using pre-specified thresholds and multiplicity control. If restricted to this dataset, the best follow-up is joint multivariable or cross-validated models adjusting for co-occurring genomic events, with pre-specified interactions, rather than more one-way subgroup strata. Priority same-dataset questions are CDKN2A versus MTAP and TP53 attribution for MDM2, IFN-gamma interaction structure for PTEN and STAT3, and whether screen quality or Cas9 activity modify core effects in formal interaction models.",
  "research_notes": "Final report. Validation exhausted and no assessments due. Accepted core dataset-specific associations: WRN/MSI R8,R39; SMARCA2/SMARCA4 R9,R26; USP7/TP53-intact R12,R40; NFE2L2/KEAP1 weaker dependency R7,R13; STAT3/PTEN R73,R79; MDM2/CDKN2A R130,R143. Negative: driver concordance null, TP53 alone not practical for MDM2/STAT3/WRN/RPL11, MYC null, ARID1A not independent SMARCA2, MTAP not robust independent predictor, PTEN specific among tested outcomes, research markers null. Unresolved: CDKN2A-MTAP/TP53 attribution, high-screen IFN interaction, some subthreshold direct strata. Next: external held-out replication or joint multivariable cross-validated models with pre-specified interactions."
